Vermont's nonconviction sealing family is terminal: 193 of 346\n\nRun 34439698619 returned RASTER_PASS for vt_seal_nonconviction-set: 2 documents, 18\npages measured, 0 problems, 0 environment problems, with the canary job and its live\nnegative controls green in the same run.\n\nBUILT_RASTER_PENDING -> COMPLETE_PACKET_PROVEN, the one transition this run. All four\nterminal conditions are now met on it: a fifteen-obligation PASS_COMPLETE_INDEPENDENT\nfrom VF25 with nine measured counters, a complete-coverage RASTER_PASS bound to these\nexact bytes, no open legal input, and a declared product wiring.\n\nThe receipt was read from the job log server-side, because the artifact blob store\nanswers 403 at this environment's egress proxy, and parsed programmatically rather\nthan transcribed. Before writing it I asserted the payload's canonical digest, its\nboundary digest and its documents digest each equal to the queued row's; the run id,\njob id and artifact id come from the jobs and artifacts APIs. Nothing here was\nretyped by hand, and the receipt records how it was read so the next reader does not\nhave to trust that sentence.\n\nThis is the family whose repair erased 1,407 dark pixels of the Judiciary's own box\nbefore FIX130 restored them, and whose fee-waiver pages VF25 measured as\npixel-identical to the Judiciary's own file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W3FAJNotS5DdvyJS1khjid","timestamp":"2026-09-10T05:17:12Z","author":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"},"committer":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"}},"repository":{"id":1248656766,"node_id":"R_kgDOSmz9fg","name":"legalease-partner-dashboard-clean","full_name":"Roger-LegalEase/legalease-partner-dashboard-clean","private":false,"owner":{"login":"Roger-LegalEase","id":287531360,"node_id":"U_kgDOESNhYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287531360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.gith